  I think this bug has been mentioned before, but I thought
I'd mention it again just to make sure.  I had a blessed mace.
I prayed, and the gods were angry.  I then did an inventory
and got the message "WARNING: prefix too short", and garbage
for the blessed mace entry.  I imagine that it became a
"cursed blessed +1 mace" and this was too long.  I later
tried to sell the mace to the shopkeeper, and the whole
game crashed after giving a message that the save file couldn't
be created, and I should notify Jeff and he might be able to
restore my game.  (Don't worry Jeff, I won't ask you to restore,
but the offer is appreciated.)

  Oh yeah, one more bug.  When I drink from a fountain as
Elbereth, and the fountain disappears, I disappear too until
I move.  OK, one final bug, the soldiers don't hilite (reverse
video, whatever).  OK, last bug I promise.  One time I was able
to step in the doorway with a load of unpaid goods, before the
shopkeeper could block it.  I was on speed (so to speak), and 
another monster was trying to get in too, but I have never been
able to do this before.

